WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.481
Hello, and welcome to week one: numbers below zero.

2
00:00:05.481 --> 00:00:10.567
By the end, you will be able to order positive and negative numbers on a number line.

3
00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.792
Let's start.

4
00:00:13.942 --> 00:00:17.959
Look at these thermometers: fridge, ice and frost.

5
00:00:17.959 --> 00:00:21.175
A thermometer shows how hot or cold it is.

6
00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:27.177
Read each thermometer: find the top of the red liquid, and read the number beside it.

7
00:00:27.177 --> 00:00:30.174
Pause the video and have a go.

8
00:00:38.824 --> 00:00:42.377
Find zero: water freezes at zero degrees.

9
00:00:42.377 --> 00:00:45.941
The fridge reads five degrees: five above zero.

10
00:00:45.941 --> 00:00:48.495
The ice reads zero degrees.

11
00:00:48.495 --> 00:00:53.557
The frost reads three below zero: we say negative three degrees.

12
00:00:53.557 --> 00:00:57.006
Say it with me: below zero is negative.

13
00:00:57.006 --> 00:00:59.533
Lower means colder.

14
00:01:01.433 --> 00:01:05.206
Now look at negative three degrees and negative eight degrees.

15
00:01:05.206 --> 00:01:09.878
Which temperature is lower?

16
00:01:09.878 --> 00:01:12.084
The lower temperature is colder.

17
00:01:12.084 --> 00:01:15.139
Pause the video and have a go.

18
00:01:23.789 --> 00:01:27.980
Both temperatures are below zero, so both are negative.

19
00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.579
Negative eight degrees is lower, so it is colder.

20
00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:37.532
Lower also means smaller: negative eight is less than negative three.

21
00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:42.358
Now the thermometer lies on its side.

22
00:01:42.358 --> 00:01:46.479
Warmer is on the right, and colder is on the left.

23
00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:49.289
The numbers under it make a number line.

24
00:01:49.289 --> 00:01:53.039
Find negative three and negative eight again:

25
00:01:53.039 --> 00:01:58.840
both are to the left of zero, and negative eight is further left.

26
00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.317
Here are some numbers on a number line.

27
00:02:03.317 --> 00:02:06.638
Read the dots from left to right to put negative eight,

28
00:02:06.638 --> 00:02:11.247
four, negative three and zero in order, smallest first.

29
00:02:11.247 --> 00:02:14.046
Pause the video and have a go.

30
00:02:22.696 --> 00:02:27.305
Say it with me: on a number line, further right means greater.

31
00:02:27.305 --> 00:02:31.322
So we read from left to right, smallest to greatest:

32
00:02:31.322 --> 00:02:35.557
negative eight, negative three, zero, four.

33
00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.106
Here is a worked example.

34
00:02:39.106 --> 00:02:46.285
Which is colder, negative four degrees or negative one degree?

35
00:02:46.285 --> 00:02:50.995
Both temperatures are below zero, so both are negative.

36
00:02:52.245 --> 00:02:57.678
Negative four degrees is lower on the thermometer, so negative four degrees is colder.

37
00:02:57.678 --> 00:03:00.593
Negative four is less than negative one.

38
00:03:00.593 --> 00:03:02.740
Pause the video.

39
00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.923
Try the next one in your booklet.

40
00:03:15.223 --> 00:03:17.150
Now let's try a question together.

41
00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:23.582
Order negative three, two, zero and negative five, from least to greatest.

42
00:03:23.582 --> 00:03:27.090
Pause the video and have a go.

43
00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:39.014
On a number line, further right means greater.

44
00:03:39.014 --> 00:03:46.653
Read the marked numbers from left to right: negative five, negative three, zero, two.

45
00:03:46.653 --> 00:03:49.962
That is the order from least to greatest.

46
00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:52.455
Well done if you got it.

47
00:03:54.355 --> 00:03:56.294
Now try it in your booklet.

48
00:03:56.294 --> 00:04:03.469
Remember: lower means colder, and on a number line, further right means greater.

49
00:04:03.469 --> 00:04:04.986
Good luck.
